        "notes": "Where the star's surface was darker and brighter in K2 campaign 2, worked out in this project from how its light rose and fell by 0.88% as it turned once in 17 days. The light curve is the mission's own; Reinhold & Hekker (2020, A&A 635, A43) found the star's rotation in it, and starry finds the map that reproduces it at their period. The longitudes of the dark and bright regions are fixed by the data; their latitudes are not. No tilt of this star's axis is known: the map is made at 60°, the middle tilt of axes that point at random.",
